                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                        "entry_id": "65a89e8c-af80-39e7-9f36-2176d4cd8452",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, pertaining to, resembling, or characteristic of rhinoceroses."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "45cc164d-6c38-48ae-8c3c-ada489f7b730",
                                "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                                "text": "Regarding us warily, the creature turned its rhinocerine head in our direction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "785eb264-4567-491c-afac-4105eee7cfb6",
                                "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                                "text": "The above appear to have been the only Rhinocerine remains discovered at Oreston..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aec5c2ad-6ccf-4d8f-b74c-3efd3914348c",
                                "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                                "text": "The old Irish pig had long legs, large, erect ears, an attenuated snout and a light body; he was a roaming, restless brute, with porcupine bristles on his back, a hide of rhinocerine thickness and an aspect grim as a wolf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "893052f5-3530-4341-9835-9c7c0ce1480b",
                                "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                                "text": "Luckily the saddlebum, following the dictates of his wit if not his predilection, snatched a fan out of his gun belt, leaned forward simpering, and tapped the enraged woman on her rhinocerine upper arm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "75d90a36-cfc5-446f-8123-5c3f7ac27b2e",
                                "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                                "text": "...to modern eyes, it is startling to see both Megalosaurus and Iguanodon depicted as extremely massive quadrupeds and the latter genus with a sharp, nasal horn. These errors were not unreasonable; rhinocerine lizards were well known to Owen (and indeed, several genera of rhinocerine dinosaurs were discovered subsequently), whereas there were no living parallels to what was, in truth, Iguanodon's spike-like thumb."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8a0ee8e-8a95-40c1-a184-8cc4d1a07271",
                                "sense_id": "8fc8f5fa-bf49-3617-96b3-25d0e497a2f2",
                                "text": "Robert Bakker first challenged the conventional view that ceratopsians' front limbs sprawled, with his own idea that their front limbs had an elephantine or rhinocerine posture."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
